Format knowledge
----------------

doctopus is an independent implementation. Its readers follow Microsoft's
Open Specifications ([MS-DOC], [MS-XLS], [MS-XLSB], [MS-PPT], [MS-VSDX],
[MS-CFB], [MS-ODRAW], [MS-OLEDS], [MS-OLEPS], [MS-OSHARED], [MS-OFFCRYPTO]),
ECMA-376 (Office Open XML), ISO 32000 (PDF) and the XMP specification
(ISO 16684-1). Where those leave details out, it relies on
what these open-source projects found:

- libvisio (https://github.com/LibreOffice/libvisio, MPL-2.0): the binary
  Visio format (.vsd), which Microsoft does not document.
- Apache POI (https://poi.apache.org, Apache-2.0): details of the binary
  Office formats, including the sheet records of workbooks written by
  beta versions of Excel 2007.

No code from these projects is included.


Test data
---------

The test corpus listed in testdata/corpus.tsv comes from Apache Tika and
Apache POI (Apache-2.0) and from libvisio (MPL-2.0). It is downloaded by
scripts/fetch-corpus.sh and is not part of this repository. The snapshots
in crates/doctopus-office/tests/snapshots and
crates/doctopus-pdf/tests/snapshots hold text extracted from those files,
which stays under the files' original licenses.


Dependencies
------------

Release binaries include third-party crates. Their licenses and notices are
in THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt next to each binary, generated by
scripts/third-party-licenses.py.

The PDF reader uses hayro (https://github.com/LaurenzV/hayro, Apache-2.0 OR
MIT), which builds data of its own into the binary:

- the standard 14 PDF fonts, from PDFium: Copyright 2014 PDFium Authors,
  original code copyright 2014 Foxit Software Inc. (BSD-3-Clause);
- Adobe's predefined CMaps: Copyright 1990-2023 Adobe (BSD-3-Clause);
- a CMYK color profile from Compact-ICC-Profiles (CC0-1.0).

Their license texts are in THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt as well.
